<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25196" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">jānĭtrix</span></b> ,
			īcis, f.
		janitor, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a female door-keeper, a portress</i>.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">anus hic solet cubitare custos, janitrix,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Curc. 1, 1, 76</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">laurus janitrix Caesarum,</span>”
				i. e. <i>planted in front of the house</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					15, 30, 39, § 127</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
